# The catalog of every variable the gateway reads. This file is committed; .env
# is not. Copy the lines you actually want to change into .env rather than the
# whole file — a .env that mirrors this one only drifts from it.
#
# Every value here is a default from internal/config/config.go — the gateway
# starts fine with this file absent. A variable already set in the real
# environment always wins over this file, so a pod or CI is never affected by
# a stray .env.
#
# Leave a line commented out to keep the default. An empty value is not the
# same as an unset one for the parsed variables: a set-but-malformed value
# fails startup on purpose.

# ── HTTP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GATEWAY_ADDR=:8080
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# REQUEST_TIMEOUT=60s
# SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=15s

# ── Failover order ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accepted names: mock, mock-flaky, mock-slow, mock-dead, bedrock, anthropic
# mock-slow hangs until PROVIDER_ATTEMPT_TIMEOUT cuts the attempt — use it to
# see what the circuit breaker actually saves (mock-dead fails too fast to show
# it).
# PROVIDERS=mock-flaky,mock

# ── Retry (total tries, not retries) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# RETRY_INITIAL_BACKOFF=100ms
# RETRY_MAX_BACKOFF=2s
# Bounds a single provider call, so a slow primary cannot eat the whole budget.
# PROVIDER_ATTEMPT_TIMEOUT=30s

# ── Circuit breaker ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BREAKER_MIN_REQUESTS=5
# BREAKER_FAILURE_RATIO=0.5
# BREAKER_OPEN_TIMEOUT=15s
# BREAKER_INTERVAL=60s

# ── Cost guard ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MAX_TOKENS=1024

# ── Bedrock (SigV4) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credentials come from the default AWS chain (env, shared file, IAM role) and
# are deliberately NOT read from our own config — do not add AWS keys here.
# BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1
# BEDROCK_MODEL=anthropic.claude-opus-5

# ── Anthropic API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one secret this file carries. Required only when PROVIDERS includes
# "anthropic". Read from the environment by the Anthropic SDK itself, not by
# internal/config — the value never enters our own structs.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5
